# Intent: The quick access sheet's Light tile (a bulb) becomes a Lock tile with a drawn padlock, still one row of six (Mute, Quiet, Lock, Apps, Games, Settings). A tap locks the unit now when a code is set, else the banner row shows "Set a code on the settings page" and the sheet stays up. The listening light switch moves to a Listening light row in Settings, General (the settings page keeps its own). The saved sheet key "light" is still read, as the same item in the same place (now the Lock tile, never twice), so a saved choice and a host that sends it keep working.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_pages_core.h, maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages_unit.cc, maipai_apps_core.h, maipai_apps.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: swipe up: one row of six tiles with a padlock where the bulb was; with no code a tap on it shows the hint in the banner row and the sheet stays, with a code (self.lock.set) a tap locks at once (self.lock.status locked true); Settings, General lists Listening light and a tap on it flips self.prefs listen_light.
# Kconfig: none

